986 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The diagram above may be used to illustrate analysis of price, abnormal profits, productive and allocative inefficiency. The analysis of the potential impact of a monopoly may include the following negative impacts The monopolist has power over price as it has the ability to be a price maker. This is because the lack of competition allows the monopolist to reduce the amount of consumer surplus The monopolist can also restrict output in order to increase price. These two features create a situation where the firm is able to earn abnormal profits and operate at levels of output which are both productively and allocatively inefficient. Abnormal profits represent a redistribution of income in favour of the entrepreneurs and away from consumers which is both inefficient and may be considered unfair/inequitable. The monopolist may also maintain barriers to entry through aggressive behaviour)
/E (The diagram above may be used to illustrate analysis of price, abnormal profits, productive and allocative inefficiency. The analysis of the potential impact of a monopoly may include the following negative impacts The monopolist has power over price as it has the ability to be a price maker. This is because the lack of competition allows the monopolist to reduce the amount of consumer surplus The monopolist can also restrict output in order to increase price. These two features create a situation where the firm is able to earn abnormal profits and operate at levels of output which are both productively and allocatively inefficient. Abnormal profits represent a redistribution of income in favour of the entrepreneurs and away from consumers which is both inefficient and may be considered unfair/inequitable. The monopolist may also maintain barriers to entry through aggressive behaviour)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
