/T (In Exemplar 5, the candidate makes a good start to this question showing a clear understanding of a perfectly contestable market, an accurate and fully integrated diagram and strong analysis of the advantages using developed chains of reasoning. Consideration of the disadvantages of a contestable market was awarded as evaluation. A common approach was to consider the impact on dynamic efficiency of lower levels of profit. This followed naturally from the diagrammatic analysis and, so, was well supported by chains of reasoning. Strong evaluation needs to include a reasoned judgement at some point in the response. Often this is attempted at the end of a response in the form of a conclusion. Lower ability candidates tend to repeat the arguments raised in their response rather than make a judgement on the balance of the arguments. Higher ability candidates are able to draw upon their arguments to show under what circumstances some arguments may be more significant than others.)
